= 33 BBY

> *"The Republic is not what it once was. The Senate is full of greedy, squabbling delegates. There is no interest in the common good."*

The Galactic Senate meets in its great rotunda on Coruscant: two thousand delegations in floating repulsorpods, speaking for a million worlds. Supreme Chancellor **Finis Valorum** governs with a fragile coalition of Core moderates, trade guilds, security-minded Colonies and assorted independents. He means well. He is also trapped by the very corruption he promised to end.

Your Caucus, about one senator in seven, sits in opposition. You are led for now by **Senator Bail Antilles of Alderaan**, a patient institutionalist, with **Garm Bel Iblis of Corellia** and **Onaconda Farr of Rodia** at his side.

In the delegation from Naboo sits a mild, courteous senator named **Palpatine**. Everyone agrees he is a decent man.

- @begin: Take your seat in the rotunda.

